A very nervous moment on the Samurai quest. I spotted
Ashikaga Takauji via telepathy immediately, but having never
been on this quest before, I didn't know how the level was
laid out and, in particular, how close I would have to get
before I could engage him. As I entered each new "ring" in
the lair, I zapped a wand of light to give a wider view of
each potential battleground.

Finally, I stepped into an opening and my /oLight revealed a
direct path to Ashikaga Takauji. Unfortunately, his henchmen
began throwing potions at me and one scored with a
!oParalysis! I was sure I would be bisected before I got
another turn. But Ashikaga Takauji didn't move during my
paralysis, maybe I wasn't close enough, only three empty
spaces, one an open door, separated us.

My first action upon recovery was to fire off my /oDeath
which somehow, strangely enough, beheaded Ashikaga Takauji.
As I stepped forward another of Ashikaga Takauji's minions
picked up a "samurai sword". I hit this foe with a /oSleep
and charged with my +6 Excalibur and +7 katana but the thief
awoke after two attacks, giving me yet another scary moment.
Fortunately, he was so near death, he turned to flee, his
last act.

Whew!
